%N A399483 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^k * H(k) * O(k) / k, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind).
%H A399483 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 9, eq. (22).
%H A399483 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-02462-8">(Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer International Publishing, 2019, section 3.20, pp. 127-131, eq. (3.114).
%H A399483 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399483 Equals Pi*G/2 - 7*zeta(3)/16 - Pi^2*log(2)/16 = A399223 - A399482, where G is Catalan's constant (A006752) (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019).
%F A399483 Equals -2 * Integral_{x=0..1} arctan(x) * log(1-x^2) / (1+x^2) dx (Vălean, 2019).
%e A399483 0.485327466680688291973437190477383524641509506615626...
%t A399483 RealDigits[Pi*Catalan/2 - 7*Zeta[3]/16 - Pi^2*Log[2]/16, 10, 120][[1]]
